IMPORT `dg-core`

-- Delaware General Corporation Law, 8 Del. C. ch. 1: Subchapter V (stock and dividends), sections 154 and 170 to 174.
-- LAYER 1: the law, objectively. The seat layer is dg3-seat.l4.
--
-- The source is the plain-text rendering de-code-t8-ch1-2026-10-01.txt of the Delaware Code Online (through 85 Del. Laws, c. 550),
-- made by a converter script. It is not the official text. `-- src:N | ...` is a slice of line N of that file; an ellipsis means the line goes on.
--
-- Units: an amount of money is a NUMBER of United States dollars. A time limit is a Period (dg-core) and dates are compared inclusively
-- (the last day of a period is inside it: Fork F10 in this piece's NOTES.md).
-- Section 154 is one of the sections that section 114(b)(1) says apply to nonstock corporations by their terms: its last sentence
-- deems the capital of a nonstock corporation to be zero for sections 154, 160 and 170, and that sentence is encoded below.
-- Sections 170 to 174 are among those from which section 114(c)(3) takes the member reading away for a nonprofit nonstock corporation.
-- Out of range: section 244 (dg5: reduction of capital), section 160 and 173 (the violations that section 174 punishes, taken as stated facts).

§ `Section 154: determination of amount of capital; capital, surplus and net assets`

-- Section 154, first and second sentences. The board may, by resolution, determine that only a part of the consideration for shares is capital.
-- If any of the shares have a par value, the part must exceed the aggregate par value of the shares that have one, unless all the shares issued are shares with par value,
-- in which case it need only equal their aggregate par value. The board shall specify the part in dollars.
-- src:500 | Any corporation may, by resolution of its board of directors, determine that only a part of the consideration which shall be received by the corporation for any of the shares of its capital stock which it shall issue from time to time shall be capital; but, in case any of the shares issued shall be shares having a par value, the amount of the part of such consideration so determined to be capital shall be in excess of the aggregate par value of the shares issued for such consideration having a par value, unless all the shares issued shall be shares having a par value, in which case the amount of the part of such consideration so determined to be capital need be only equal to the aggregate par value of such shares. In each such case the board of directors shall specify in dollars the part of such consideration which shall be capital. If the board of directors shall not have determined (1) at the time of issue of any shares of the capital stock of the corporation issued for cash or (2) within 60 days after the issue of any shares of the capital stock of the corporation issued for consideration other than cash what part of the consideration for such shares shall be capital, the capital of the corporation in respect of such shares shall be an amount equal to the aggregate par value of such shares having a par value, plus the amount of the consideration for such shares without par value. The amount of the consideration so determined to be capital in respect of any shares without par value shall be the stated capital of such shares. The capital of the corporation may be increased from time to time by resolution of the board of directors directing that a portion of the net assets of the corporation in excess of the amount so determined to be capital be transferred to the capital account. The board of directors may direct that the portion of such net assets so transferred shall be treated as capital in respect of any shares of the corporation of any designated class or classes. The excess, if any, at any given time, of the net assets of the corporation over the amount so determined to be capital shall be surplus. Net assets means the amount by which total assets exceed total liabilities. Capital and surplus are not liabilities for this purpose. Notwithstanding anything in this section to the contrary, for purposes of this section and §§ 160 and 170 of this title, the capital of any nonstock corporation shall be deemed to be zero.
-- src:500 | In each such case the board of directors shall specify in dollars the part of such consideration which shall be capital. If the board of directors shall not have determined (1) at the time of issue of any shares of the capital stock of the corporation issued for cash or (2) within 60 days after the issue of any shares of the capital stock of the corporation issued for consideration other than cash what part of the consideration for such shares shall be capital, the capital of the corporation in respect of such shares shall be an amount equal to the aggregate par value of such shares having a par value, plus the amount of the consideration for such shares without par value. The amount of the consideration so determined to be capital in respect of any shares without par value shall be the stated capital of such shares. The capital of the corporation may be increased from time to time by resolution of the board of directors directing that a portion of the net assets of the corporation in excess of the amount so determined to be capital be transferred to the capital account. The board of directors may direct that the portion of such net assets so transferred shall be treated as capital in respect of any shares of the corporation of any designated class or classes. The excess, if any, at any given time, of the net assets of the corporation over the amount so determined to be capital shall be surplus. Net assets means the amount by which total assets exceed total liabilities. Capital and surplus are not liabilities for this purpose. Notwithstanding anything in this section to the contrary, for purposes of this section and §§ 160 and 170 of this title, the capital of any nonstock corporation shall be deemed to be zero.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 154 (src:500)
DECLARE `s 154 A determination by the board of the part that is capital` HAS
    `the amount in dollars the board determined to be capital` IS A NUMBER
    `the day the board determined it`                          IS A DATE

@ref 8 Del. C. § 154 (src:500)
DECLARE `s 154 Facts about the capital for shares issued` HAS
    `the consideration received for the shares`                                    IS A NUMBER
    `the aggregate par value of the shares having a par value`                     IS A NUMBER
    `the consideration for the shares without par value`                           IS A NUMBER
    `all the shares issued for the consideration are shares having a par value`    IS A BOOLEAN
    `the shares were issued for cash`                                              IS A BOOLEAN
    `the day the shares were issued`                                               IS A DATE
    `the determination of the board, if it made one`                               IS A MAYBE `s 154 A determination by the board of the part that is capital`

-- The permitted size of the part determined to be capital: more than the aggregate par value of the shares with par value,
-- or, when all the shares issued are shares with par value, at least that value; and a part of the consideration, so no more than the consideration received.
-- src:500 | the amount of the part of such consideration so determined to be capital shall be in excess of the aggregate par value of the shares issued for such consideration having a par value, unless all the shares issued shall be shares having a par value, in which case the amount of the part of such consideration so determined to be capital need be only equal to the aggregate par value of such shares. In each such case the board of directors shall specify in dollars the part of such consideration which shall be capital. If the board of directors shall not have determined (1) at the time of issue of any shares of the capital stock of the corporation issued for cash or (2) within 60 days after the issue of any shares of the capital stock of the corporation issued for consideration other than cash what part of the consideration for such shares shall be capital, the capital of the corporation in respect of such shares shall be an amount equal to the aggregate par value of such shares having a par value, plus the amount of the consideration for such shares without par value. The amount of the consideration so determined to be capital in respect of any shares without par value shall be the stated capital of such shares. The capital of the corporation may be increased from time to time by resolution of the board of directors directing that a portion of the net assets of the corporation in excess of the amount so determined to be capital be transferred to the capital account. The board of directors may direct that the portion of such net assets so transferred shall be treated as capital in respect of any shares of the corporation of any designated class or classes. The excess, if any, at any given time, of the net assets of the corporation over the amount so determined to be capital shall be surplus. Net assets means the amount by which total assets exceed total liabilities. Capital and surplus are not liabilities for this purpose. Notwithstanding anything in this section to the contrary, for purposes of this section and §§ 160 and 170 of this title, the capital of any nonstock corporation shall be deemed to be zero.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 154 (src:500)
GIVEN f IS A `s 154 Facts about the capital for shares issued`
      amount IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 154 the amount the board determined is a permitted part of the consideration` f amount MEANS
        IF f's `all the shares issued for the consideration are shares having a par value`
        THEN amount AT LEAST (f's `the aggregate par value of the shares having a par value`)
        ELSE amount GREATER THAN (f's `the aggregate par value of the shares having a par value`)
    AND amount AT MOST (f's `the consideration received for the shares`)

-- Section 154, third sentence. If the board has not determined the part (1) at the time of issue, for shares issued for cash, or (2) within 60 days after the issue,
-- for shares issued for other consideration, the capital in respect of the shares is the aggregate par value of the shares with par value plus the consideration for the shares without par value.
-- "At the time of issue" is read as no later than the day of issue (Fork F3); "within 60 days after the issue" as no later than the 60th day after it (Fork F10).
-- src:500 | If the board of directors shall not have determined (1) at the time of issue of any shares of the capital stock of the corporation issued for cash or (2) within 60 days after the issue of any shares of the capital stock of the corporation issued for consideration other than cash what part of the consideration for such shares shall be capital, the capital of the corporation in respect of such shares shall be an amount equal to the aggregate par value of such shares having a par value, plus the amount of the consideration for such shares without par value. The amount of the consideration so determined to be capital in respect of any shares without par value shall be the stated capital of such shares. The capital of the corporation may be increased from time to time by resolution of the board of directors directing that a portion of the net assets of the corporation in excess of the amount so determined to be capital be transferred to the capital account. The board of directors may direct that the portion of such net assets so transferred shall be treated as capital in respect of any shares of the corporation of any designated class or classes. The excess, if any, at any given time, of the net assets of the corporation over the amount so determined to be capital shall be surplus. Net assets means the amount by which total assets exceed total liabilities. Capital and surplus are not liabilities for this purpose. Notwithstanding anything in this section to the contrary, for purposes of this section and §§ 160 and 170 of this title, the capital of any nonstock corporation shall be deemed to be zero.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 154 (src:500)
GIVEN f IS A `s 154 Facts about the capital for shares issued`
GIVETH A `Period`
`s 154 the time allowed for the board's determination` f MEANS
    IF f's `the shares were issued for cash`
    THEN `period in days` 0
    ELSE `period in days` 60

@ref 8 Del. C. § 154 (src:500)
GIVEN f IS A `s 154 Facts about the capital for shares issued`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 154 the capital in respect of the shares if the board did not determine it in time` f MEANS
    (f's `the aggregate par value of the shares having a par value`) PLUS (f's `the consideration for the shares without par value`)

-- The capital in respect of the shares: the part the board determined in time, if that part is a permitted one; otherwise (no determination, or one made too late) the amount above.
-- A determination made in time but not permitted by the section is a case the text does not answer: NOTHING.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 154 (src:500)
GIVEN f IS A `s 154 Facts about the capital for shares issued`
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 154 the capital in respect of the shares` f MEANS
    CONSIDER f's `the determination of the board, if it made one`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN JUST (`s 154 the capital in respect of the shares if the board did not determine it in time` f)
    WHEN JUST d THEN
        IF (d's `the day the board determined it`) AT MOST (`the date` (`s 154 the time allowed for the board's determination` f) `after` (f's `the day the shares were issued`))
        THEN (IF `s 154 the amount the board determined is a permitted part of the consideration` f (d's `the amount in dollars the board determined to be capital`)
              THEN JUST (d's `the amount in dollars the board determined to be capital`)
              ELSE NOTHING)
        ELSE JUST (`s 154 the capital in respect of the shares if the board did not determine it in time` f)

-- The amount of the consideration determined to be capital in respect of shares without par value is the stated capital of those shares.
-- src:500 | The amount of the consideration so determined to be capital in respect of any shares without par value shall be the stated capital of such shares. The capital of the corporation may be increased from time to time by resolution of the board of directors directing that a portion of the net assets of the corporation in excess of the amount so determined to be capital be transferred to the capital account. The board of directors may direct that the portion of such net assets so transferred shall be treated as capital in respect of any shares of the corporation of any designated class or classes. The excess, if any, at any given time, of the net assets of the corporation over the amount so determined to be capital shall be surplus. Net assets means the amount by which total assets exceed total liabilities. Capital and surplus are not liabilities for this purpose. Notwithstanding anything in this section to the contrary, for purposes of this section and §§ 160 and 170 of this title, the capital of any nonstock corporation shall be deemed to be zero.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 154 (src:500)
GIVEN `the amount of the consideration determined to be capital in respect of the shares without par value` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 154 the stated capital of the shares without par value` `the amount of the consideration determined to be capital in respect of the shares without par value` MEANS
    `the amount of the consideration determined to be capital in respect of the shares without par value`

-- The capital may be increased by a board resolution directing that a portion of the net assets in excess of the amount so determined to be capital be transferred to the capital account;
-- the portion transferred may be treated as capital in respect of the shares of any designated class or classes.
-- A portion larger than the net assets in excess of capital is a case the text does not answer: NOTHING.
-- src:500 | The capital of the corporation may be increased from time to time by resolution of the board of directors directing that a portion of the net assets of the corporation in excess of the amount so determined to be capital be transferred to the capital account. The board of directors may direct that the portion of such net assets so transferred shall be treated as capital in respect of any shares of the corporation of any designated class or classes. The excess, if any, at any given time, of the net assets of the corporation over the amount so determined to be capital shall be surplus. Net assets means the amount by which total assets exceed total liabilities. Capital and surplus are not liabilities for this purpose. Notwithstanding anything in this section to the contrary, for purposes of this section and §§ 160 and 170 of this title, the capital of any nonstock corporation shall be deemed to be zero.
-- src:500 | The board of directors may direct that the portion of such net assets so transferred shall be treated as capital in respect of any shares of the corporation of any designated class or classes. The excess, if any, at any given time, of the net assets of the corporation over the amount so determined to be capital shall be surplus. Net assets means the amount by which total assets exceed total liabilities. Capital and surplus are not liabilities for this purpose. Notwithstanding anything in this section to the contrary, for purposes of this section and §§ 160 and 170 of this title, the capital of any nonstock corporation shall be deemed to be zero.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 154 (src:500)
GIVEN `the capital before the transfer` IS A NUMBER
      `the net assets of the corporation` IS A NUMBER
      `the portion of the net assets the board directs be transferred to the capital account` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 154 the capital after a transfer from the net assets` `the capital before the transfer` `the net assets of the corporation` `the portion of the net assets the board directs be transferred to the capital account` MEANS
    IF     (`the portion of the net assets the board directs be transferred to the capital account` AT LEAST 0)
       AND (`the portion of the net assets the board directs be transferred to the capital account` AT MOST ((`the net assets of the corporation`) MINUS (`the capital before the transfer`)))
    THEN JUST (`the capital before the transfer` PLUS `the portion of the net assets the board directs be transferred to the capital account`)
    ELSE NOTHING

-- Net assets means the amount by which total assets exceed total liabilities; capital and surplus are not liabilities for this purpose,
-- so the total liabilities taken here are those without capital and surplus.
-- src:500 | Net assets means the amount by which total assets exceed total liabilities. Capital and surplus are not liabilities for this purpose. Notwithstanding anything in this section to the contrary, for purposes of this section and §§ 160 and 170 of this title, the capital of any nonstock corporation shall be deemed to be zero.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 154 (src:500)
GIVEN `the total assets of the corporation` IS A NUMBER
      `the total liabilities of the corporation, not counting capital and surplus` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 154 the net assets of the corporation` `the total assets of the corporation` `the total liabilities of the corporation, not counting capital and surplus` MEANS
    `the total assets of the corporation` MINUS `the total liabilities of the corporation, not counting capital and surplus`

-- The excess, if any, at any given time, of the net assets over the amount determined to be capital is surplus. No excess means no surplus: NOTHING.
-- src:500 | The excess, if any, at any given time, of the net assets of the corporation over the amount so determined to be capital shall be surplus. Net assets means the amount by which total assets exceed total liabilities. Capital and surplus are not liabilities for this purpose. Notwithstanding anything in this section to the contrary, for purposes of this section and §§ 160 and 170 of this title, the capital of any nonstock corporation shall be deemed to be zero.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 154 (src:500)
GIVEN `the net assets of the corporation` IS A NUMBER
      `the capital of the corporation` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 154 the surplus of the corporation, if any` `the net assets of the corporation` `the capital of the corporation` MEANS
    IF `the net assets of the corporation` GREATER THAN `the capital of the corporation`
    THEN JUST (`the net assets of the corporation` MINUS `the capital of the corporation`)
    ELSE NOTHING

-- Notwithstanding anything else in the section, for sections 154, 160 and 170 the capital of any nonstock corporation is deemed to be zero.
-- src:500 | Notwithstanding anything in this section to the contrary, for purposes of this section and §§ 160 and 170 of this title, the capital of any nonstock corporation shall be deemed to be zero.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 154 (src:500)
GIVEN k IS A `Kind of corporation`
      `the capital determined as for a stock corporation` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 154 the capital to use in sections 154, 160 and 170` k `the capital determined as for a stock corporation` MEANS
    IF `the kind is a nonstock corporation` k
    THEN 0
    ELSE `the capital determined as for a stock corporation`

§ `Section 170: dividends; payment; wasting asset corporations`

-- The facts about a proposed dividend, for section 170(a).
-- src:587 | The directors of every corporation, subject to any restrictions contained in its certificate of incorporation, may declare and pay dividends upon the shares of its capital stock either:
@ref 8 Del. C. § 170(a) (src:587)
DECLARE `s 170(a) Facts about a proposed dividend` HAS
    `the restrictions in the certificate of incorporation allow the dividend`                                  IS A BOOLEAN
    `the amount of the dividend`                                                                              IS A NUMBER
    `the surplus, if any, as defined in and computed in accordance with sections 154 and 244`                IS A MAYBE NUMBER
    `the net profits for the fiscal year in which the dividend is declared`                                   IS A NUMBER
    `the net profits for the preceding fiscal year`                                                           IS A NUMBER
    `the capital computed in accordance with sections 154 and 244`                                            IS A NUMBER
    `the aggregate amount of the capital represented by the issued and outstanding stock of all classes having a preference upon the distribution of assets` IS A NUMBER

-- (a)(1): the dividend may be paid out of surplus.
-- src:588 | Out of its surplus, as defined in and computed in accordance with §§ 154 and 244 of this title; or
@ref 8 Del. C. § 170(a)(1) (src:588)
GIVEN p IS A `s 170(a) Facts about a proposed dividend`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 170(a)(1) the dividend can be paid out of surplus` p MEANS
    CONSIDER p's `the surplus, if any, as defined in and computed in accordance with sections 154 and 244`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST surplus THEN ((p's `the amount of the dividend`) AT MOST surplus)

-- (a)(2) is read literally: "in case there shall be no such surplus" opens this route only when there is no surplus at all; if some surplus exists but is less than the dividend, neither route is open (Fork F16).
-- (a)(2): in case there is no such surplus, out of the net profits for the fiscal year in which the dividend is declared and/or the preceding fiscal year;
-- but if the capital has been diminished below the capital represented by the outstanding stock having a preference on distribution of assets,
-- no dividend on any class may be declared and paid out of such net profits until the deficiency is repaired.
-- src:589 | In case there shall be no such surplus, out of its net profits for the fiscal year in which the dividend is declared and/or the preceding fiscal year.
-- src:590 | If the capital of the corporation, computed in accordance with §§ 154 and 244 of this title, shall have been diminished by depreciation in the value of its property, or by losses, or otherwise, to an amount less than the aggregate amount of the capital represented by the issued and outstanding stock of all classes having a preference upon the distribution of assets, the directors of such corporation shall not declare and pay out of such net profits any dividends upon any shares of any classes of its capital stock until the deficiency in the amount of capital represented by the issued and outstanding stock of all classes having a preference upon the distribution of assets shall have been repaired. Nothing in this subsection shall invalidate or otherwise affect a note, debenture or other obligation of the corporation paid by it as a dividend on shares of its stock, or any payment made thereon, if at the time such note, debenture or obligation was delivered by the corporation, the corporation had either surplus or net profits as provided in (a)(1) or (2) of this section from which the dividend could lawfully have been paid.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 170(a)(2) (src:589-590)
GIVEN p IS A `s 170(a) Facts about a proposed dividend`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 170(a)(2) the dividend can be paid out of net profits` p MEANS
        (    CONSIDER p's `the surplus, if any, as defined in and computed in accordance with sections 154 and 244`
             WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE
             WHEN JUST surplus THEN FALSE)
    AND ((p's `the amount of the dividend`) AT MOST ((p's `the net profits for the fiscal year in which the dividend is declared`) PLUS (p's `the net profits for the preceding fiscal year`)))
    AND ((p's `the capital computed in accordance with sections 154 and 244`) AT LEAST (p's `the aggregate amount of the capital represented by the issued and outstanding stock of all classes having a preference upon the distribution of assets`))

-- The directors, subject to any restrictions in the certificate, may declare and pay the dividend out of surplus or, if there is none, out of net profits.
-- src:587 | The directors of every corporation, subject to any restrictions contained in its certificate of incorporation, may declare and pay dividends upon the shares of its capital stock either:
@ref 8 Del. C. § 170(a) (src:587)
GIVEN p IS A `s 170(a) Facts about a proposed dividend`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 170(a) the directors may declare and pay the dividend` p MEANS
        p's `the restrictions in the certificate of incorporation allow the dividend`
    AND (    `s 170(a)(1) the dividend can be paid out of surplus` p
         OR  `s 170(a)(2) the dividend can be paid out of net profits` p)

-- Nothing in subsection (a) invalidates or affects a note, debenture or other obligation paid as a dividend, or any payment on it, if when it was delivered
-- the corporation had either surplus or net profits from which the dividend could lawfully have been paid under (a)(1) or (2).
-- src:590 | Nothing in this subsection shall invalidate or otherwise affect a note, debenture or other obligation of the corporation paid by it as a dividend on shares of its stock, or any payment made thereon, if at the time such note, debenture or obligation was delivered by the corporation, the corporation had either surplus or net profits as provided in (a)(1) or (2) of this section from which the dividend could lawfully have been paid.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 170(a) (src:590)
GIVEN `at the time the note, debenture or obligation was delivered the corporation had surplus or net profits from which the dividend could lawfully have been paid under subsection (a)(1) or (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 170(a) the note, debenture or obligation paid as a dividend remains valid` `at the time the note, debenture or obligation was delivered the corporation had surplus or net profits from which the dividend could lawfully have been paid under subsection (a)(1) or (2)` MEANS
    `at the time the note, debenture or obligation was delivered the corporation had surplus or net profits from which the dividend could lawfully have been paid under subsection (a)(1) or (2)`

-- Section 170(b): subject to any restriction in its certificate, the directors of a corporation engaged in the exploitation of wasting assets
-- (natural resources, patents) or primarily in the liquidation of specific assets may determine the net profits, or the net proceeds of the liquidation,
-- without taking into consideration the depletion of those assets resulting from lapse of time, consumption, liquidation or exploitation.
-- src:591 | Subject to any restrictions contained in its certificate of incorporation, the directors of any corporation engaged in the exploitation of wasting assets (including but not limited to a corporation engaged in the exploitation of natural resources or other wasting assets, including patents, or engaged primarily in the liquidation of specific assets) may determine the net profits derived from the exploitation of such wasting assets or the net proceeds derived from such liquidation without taking into consideration the depletion of such assets resulting from lapse of time, consumption, liquidation or exploitation of such assets.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 170(b) (src:591)
GIVEN `the corporation is engaged in the exploitation of wasting assets or primarily in the liquidation of specific assets` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a restriction in the certificate of incorporation forbids determining the net profits without regard to depletion` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 170(b) the directors may determine the net profits without taking depletion into consideration` `the corporation is engaged in the exploitation of wasting assets or primarily in the liquidation of specific assets` `a restriction in the certificate of incorporation forbids determining the net profits without regard to depletion` MEANS
        `the corporation is engaged in the exploitation of wasting assets or primarily in the liquidation of specific assets`
    AND (NOT `a restriction in the certificate of incorporation forbids determining the net profits without regard to depletion`)

§ `Section 171: special purpose reserves`

-- The directors may set apart out of any funds available for dividends a reserve or reserves for any proper purpose, and may abolish any such reserve.
-- Whether the purpose is "proper" is a judgment: an input.
-- src:595 | The directors of a corporation may set apart out of any of the funds of the corporation available for dividends a reserve or reserves for any proper purpose and may abolish any such reserve.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 171 (src:595)
GIVEN `the funds are available for dividends` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the purpose is a proper purpose` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 171 the directors may set apart a reserve` `the funds are available for dividends` `the purpose is a proper purpose` MEANS
        `the funds are available for dividends`
    AND `the purpose is a proper purpose`

-- src:595 | and may abolish any such reserve.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 171 (src:595)
GIVEN `the reserve was set apart under section 171` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 171 the directors may abolish the reserve` `the reserve was set apart under section 171` MEANS
    `the reserve was set apart under section 171`

§ `Section 172: liability of directors and committee members as to dividends or stock redemption`

-- What a director or committee member relied on.
-- src:599 | upon the records of the corporation and upon such information, opinions, reports or statements presented to the corporation by any of its officers or employees, or committees of the board of directors, or by any other person as to matters the director reasonably believes are within such other person’s professional or expert competence and who has been selected with reasonable care by or on behalf of the corporation, as to the value and amount of the assets, liabilities and/or net profits of the corporation or any other facts pertinent to the existence and amount of surplus or other funds from which dividends might properly be declared and paid, or with which the corporation’s stock might properly be purchased or redeemed.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 172 (src:599)
DECLARE `s 172 What the director relied on` IS ONE OF
    `the records of the corporation under s 172`
    `information, opinions, reports or statements presented by an officer or employee under s 172`
    `information, opinions, reports or statements presented by a committee of the board under s 172`
    `information, opinions, reports or statements presented by any other person under s 172`

@ref 8 Del. C. § 172 (src:599)
DECLARE `s 172 Reliance by a director or committee member` HAS
    `the person is a member of the board of directors or of a committee designated by the board` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person relied in good faith`                                                          IS A BOOLEAN
    `what the person relied on`                                                                IS A `s 172 What the director relied on`
    `the person reasonably believes the matters are within the other person's professional or expert competence` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the other person was selected with reasonable care by or on behalf of the corporation`    IS A BOOLEAN
    `the matter is the value and amount of the assets, liabilities or net profits of the corporation, or another fact pertinent to the existence and amount of surplus or other funds from which dividends might properly be declared and paid, or with which the corporation's stock might properly be purchased or redeemed` IS A BOOLEAN

-- A member of the board, or of a committee designated by the board, is fully protected in relying in good faith on the corporation's records and on the information, opinions, reports or statements
-- presented by its officers or employees, by committees of the board, or by any other person as to matters the director reasonably believes are within that person's professional or expert competence
-- and who has been selected with reasonable care by or on behalf of the corporation, as to the value and amount of the assets, liabilities or net profits or other facts pertinent to surplus or other funds.
-- The two conditions about the "other person" are read as attaching to "any other person" only (Fork F6).
-- src:599 | A member of the board of directors, or a member of any committee designated by the board of directors, shall be fully protected in relying in good faith upon the records of the corporation and upon such information, opinions, reports or statements presented to the corporation by any of its officers or employees, or committees of the board of directors, or by any other person as to matters the director reasonably believes are within such other person’s professional or expert competence and who has been selected with reasonable care by or on behalf of the corporation, as to the value and amount of the assets, liabilities and/or net profits of the corporation or any other facts pertinent to the existence and amount of surplus or other funds from which dividends might properly be declared and paid, or with which the corporation’s stock might properly be purchased or redeemed.
-- src:599 | or by any other person as to matters the director reasonably believes are within such other person’s professional or expert competence and who has been selected with reasonable care by or on behalf of the corporation, as to the value and amount of the assets, liabilities and/or net profits of the corporation or any other facts pertinent to the existence and amount of surplus or other funds from which dividends might properly be declared and paid, or with which the corporation’s stock might properly be purchased or redeemed.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 172 (src:599)
GIVEN r IS A `s 172 Reliance by a director or committee member`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 172 the director or committee member is fully protected` r MEANS
        r's `the person is a member of the board of directors or of a committee designated by the board`
    AND r's `the person relied in good faith`
    AND r's `the matter is the value and amount of the assets, liabilities or net profits of the corporation, or another fact pertinent to the existence and amount of surplus or other funds from which dividends might properly be declared and paid, or with which the corporation's stock might properly be purchased or redeemed`
    AND (    CONSIDER r's `what the person relied on`
             WHEN `the records of the corporation under s 172` THEN TRUE
             WHEN `information, opinions, reports or statements presented by an officer or employee under s 172` THEN TRUE
             WHEN `information, opinions, reports or statements presented by a committee of the board under s 172` THEN TRUE
             WHEN `information, opinions, reports or statements presented by any other person under s 172` THEN
                     (    r's `the person reasonably believes the matters are within the other person's professional or expert competence`
                      AND r's `the other person was selected with reasonable care by or on behalf of the corporation`))

§ `Section 173: declaration and payment of dividends`

-- The forms in which a dividend may be paid.
-- src:603 | Dividends may be paid in cash, in property, or in shares of the corporation’s capital stock. If the dividend is to be paid in shares of the corporation’s theretofore unissued capital stock the board of directors shall, by resolution, direct that there be designated as capital in respect of such shares an amount which is not less than the aggregate par value of par value shares being declared as a dividend and, in the case of shares without par value being declared as a dividend, such amount as shall be determined by the board of directors. No such designation as capital shall be necessary if shares are being distributed by a corporation pursuant to a split-up or division of its stock rather than as payment of a dividend declared payable in stock of the corporation.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 173 (src:603)
DECLARE `s 173 The form of a dividend` IS ONE OF
    `a dividend in cash under s 173`
    `a dividend in property under s 173`
    `a dividend in shares of the capital stock of the corporation under s 173`
    `a dividend in another form under s 173`

-- No corporation shall pay dividends except in accordance with the chapter. Dividends may be paid in cash, in property, or in shares of the corporation's capital stock.
-- A dividend in another form is a case the text does not answer: NOTHING.
-- src:603 | No corporation shall pay dividends except in accordance with this chapter. Dividends may be paid in cash, in property, or in shares of the corporation’s capital stock. If the dividend is to be paid in shares of the corporation’s theretofore unissued capital stock the board of directors shall, by resolution, direct that there be designated as capital in respect of such shares an amount which is not less than the aggregate par value of par value shares being declared as a dividend and, in the case of shares without par value being declared as a dividend, such amount as shall be determined by the board of directors. No such designation as capital shall be necessary if shares are being distributed by a corporation pursuant to a split-up or division of its stock rather than as payment of a dividend declared payable in stock of the corporation.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 173 (src:603)
GIVEN `the payment is in accordance with this chapter` IS A BOOLEAN
      form IS A `s 173 The form of a dividend`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 173 the corporation may pay the dividend` `the payment is in accordance with this chapter` form MEANS
    CONSIDER form
    WHEN `a dividend in another form under s 173` THEN NOTHING
    OTHERWISE JUST `the payment is in accordance with this chapter`

-- If the dividend is to be paid in shares of the corporation's theretofore unissued capital stock, the board shall by resolution direct that there be designated as capital
-- an amount not less than the aggregate par value of the par value shares declared as a dividend and, for shares without par value, such amount as the board determines.
-- No designation is necessary if the shares are distributed in a split-up or division of the stock rather than as payment of a dividend declared payable in stock.
-- src:603 | If the dividend is to be paid in shares of the corporation’s theretofore unissued capital stock the board of directors shall, by resolution, direct that there be designated as capital in respect of such shares an amount which is not less than the aggregate par value of par value shares being declared as a dividend and, in the case of shares without par value being declared as a dividend, such amount as shall be determined by the board of directors. No such designation as capital shall be necessary if shares are being distributed by a corporation pursuant to a split-up or division of its stock rather than as payment of a dividend declared payable in stock of the corporation.
-- src:603 | No such designation as capital shall be necessary if shares are being distributed by a corporation pursuant to a split-up or division of its stock rather than as payment of a dividend declared payable in stock of the corporation.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 173 (src:603)
GIVEN `the shares are distributed in a split-up or division of the stock rather than as payment of a dividend declared payable in stock` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the board directed by resolution that an amount be designated as capital` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amount designated as capital` IS A NUMBER
      `the aggregate par value of the par value shares being declared as a dividend` IS A NUMBER
      `the board determined the amount designated for the shares without par value` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there are shares without par value among the shares declared as a dividend` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 173 the designation as capital for a dividend in shares is as the section requires` `the shares are distributed in a split-up or division of the stock rather than as payment of a dividend declared payable in stock` `the board directed by resolution that an amount be designated as capital` `the amount designated as capital` `the aggregate par value of the par value shares being declared as a dividend` `the board determined the amount designated for the shares without par value` `there are shares without par value among the shares declared as a dividend` MEANS
        `the shares are distributed in a split-up or division of the stock rather than as payment of a dividend declared payable in stock`
    OR  (    `the board directed by resolution that an amount be designated as capital`
         AND (`the amount designated as capital` AT LEAST `the aggregate par value of the par value shares being declared as a dividend`)
         AND (    (NOT `there are shares without par value among the shares declared as a dividend`)
              OR  `the board determined the amount designated for the shares without par value`))

§ `Section 174: liability of directors for unlawful payment of dividend or unlawful stock purchase or redemption`

-- The facts about one director and one unlawful dividend, purchase or redemption, for section 174(a).
-- src:607 | In case of any wilful or negligent violation of § 160 or § 173 of this title, the directors under whose administration the same may happen shall be jointly and severally liable, at any time within 6 years after paying such unlawful dividend or after such unlawful stock purchase or redemption, to the corporation, and to its creditors in the event of its dissolution or insolvency, to the full amount of the dividend unlawfully paid, or to the full amount unlawfully paid for the purchase or redemption of the corporation’s stock, with interest from the time such liability accrued. Any director who may have been absent when the same was done, or who may have dissented from the act or resolution by which the same was done, may be exonerated from such liability by causing his or her dissent to be entered on the books containing the minutes of the proceedings of the directors at the time the same was done, or immediately after such director has notice of the same.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 174(a) (src:607)
DECLARE `s 174(a) Facts about a director and an unlawful payment` HAS
    `the dividend, purchase or redemption violated section 160 or section 173`            IS A BOOLEAN
    `the violation was wilful or negligent`                                              IS A BOOLEAN
    `the director was a director under whose administration it happened`                 IS A BOOLEAN
    `the day the unlawful dividend was paid or the unlawful purchase or redemption was made` IS A DATE
    `the day the claim is made`                                                          IS A DATE
    `the director was absent when it was done or dissented from the act or resolution`   IS A BOOLEAN
    `the director caused the dissent to be entered on the books containing the minutes of the proceedings of the directors at the time it was done or immediately after the director had notice of it` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the corporation is dissolved or insolvent`                                          IS A BOOLEAN

-- A director who was absent, or who dissented, may be exonerated by causing the dissent to be entered on the books containing the minutes at the time, or immediately after notice.
-- src:607 | Any director who may have been absent when the same was done, or who may have dissented from the act or resolution by which the same was done, may be exonerated from such liability by causing his or her dissent to be entered on the books containing the minutes of the proceedings of the directors at the time the same was done, or immediately after such director has notice of the same.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 174(a) (src:607)
GIVEN f IS A `s 174(a) Facts about a director and an unlawful payment`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 174(a) the director is exonerated from the liability` f MEANS
        f's `the director was absent when it was done or dissented from the act or resolution`
    AND f's `the director caused the dissent to be entered on the books containing the minutes of the proceedings of the directors at the time it was done or immediately after the director had notice of it`

-- The directors under whose administration a wilful or negligent violation of section 160 or 173 happens are jointly and severally liable, at any time within 6 years after the payment,
-- purchase or redemption, to the corporation, and to its creditors in the event of its dissolution or insolvency, unless exonerated.
-- src:607 | at any time within 6 years after paying such unlawful dividend or after such unlawful stock purchase or redemption, to the corporation, and to its creditors in the event of its dissolution or insolvency, to the full amount of the dividend unlawfully paid, or to the full amount unlawfully paid for the purchase or redemption of the corporation’s stock, with interest from the time such liability accrued. Any director who may have been absent when the same was done, or who may have dissented from the act or resolution by which the same was done, may be exonerated from such liability by causing his or her dissent to be entered on the books containing the minutes of the proceedings of the directors at the time the same was done, or immediately after such director has notice of the same.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 174(a) (src:607)
GIVEN f IS A `s 174(a) Facts about a director and an unlawful payment`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 174(a) the director is liable to the corporation` f MEANS
        f's `the dividend, purchase or redemption violated section 160 or section 173`
    AND f's `the violation was wilful or negligent`
    AND f's `the director was a director under whose administration it happened`
    AND ((f's `the day the claim is made`) AT MOST (`the date` (`period in years` 6) `after` (f's `the day the unlawful dividend was paid or the unlawful purchase or redemption was made`)))
    AND (NOT `s 174(a) the director is exonerated from the liability` f)

@ref 8 Del. C. § 174(a) (src:607)
GIVEN f IS A `s 174(a) Facts about a director and an unlawful payment`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 174(a) the director is liable to the creditors of the corporation` f MEANS
        `s 174(a) the director is liable to the corporation` f
    AND f's `the corporation is dissolved or insolvent`

-- The liability is to the full amount of the dividend unlawfully paid, or of the amount unlawfully paid for the purchase or redemption, with interest from the time the liability accrued.
-- The text does not fix the rate: the interest is an input.
-- src:607 | to the full amount of the dividend unlawfully paid, or to the full amount unlawfully paid for the purchase or redemption of the corporation’s stock, with interest from the time such liability accrued. Any director who may have been absent when the same was done, or who may have dissented from the act or resolution by which the same was done, may be exonerated from such liability by causing his or her dissent to be entered on the books containing the minutes of the proceedings of the directors at the time the same was done, or immediately after such director has notice of the same.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 174(a) (src:607)
GIVEN `the full amount of the dividend unlawfully paid or unlawfully paid for the purchase or redemption` IS A NUMBER
      `the interest from the time the liability accrued` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 174(a) the amount for which the directors are liable` `the full amount of the dividend unlawfully paid or unlawfully paid for the purchase or redemption` `the interest from the time the liability accrued` MEANS
    `the full amount of the dividend unlawfully paid or unlawfully paid for the purchase or redemption` PLUS `the interest from the time the liability accrued`

-- Section 174(b): a director against whom a claim is successfully asserted is entitled to contribution from the other directors who voted for or concurred in the unlawful dividend, purchase or redemption.
-- The text does not say in what proportions: this rule says only who owes contribution.
-- src:608 | Any director against whom a claim is successfully asserted under this section shall be entitled to contribution from the other directors who voted for or concurred in the unlawful dividend, stock purchase or stock redemption.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 174(b) (src:608)
GIVEN `a claim has been successfully asserted against the director under section 174` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the other director voted for or concurred in the unlawful dividend, stock purchase or stock redemption` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 174(b) the other director owes contribution to the director` `a claim has been successfully asserted against the director under section 174` `the other director voted for or concurred in the unlawful dividend, stock purchase or stock redemption` MEANS
        `a claim has been successfully asserted against the director under section 174`
    AND `the other director voted for or concurred in the unlawful dividend, stock purchase or stock redemption`

-- Section 174(c): to the extent of the amount the director paid on the claim, the director is subrogated to the corporation's rights against the stockholders who received the dividend, or assets for the sale or redemption
-- of their stock, with knowledge of facts indicating it was unlawful, in proportion to the amounts those stockholders received. NOTHING for a stockholder who did not receive it with that knowledge,
-- or when the director has not been successfully pursued, or when the amounts received cannot be a proportion (the knowing stockholders received 0 or less in all).
-- The text does not cap the share at what the stockholder received (Fork F7).
-- src:609 | Any director against whom a claim is successfully asserted under this section shall be entitled, to the extent of the amount paid by such director as a result of such claim, to be subrogated to the rights of the corporation against stockholders who received the dividend on, or assets for the sale or redemption of, their stock with knowledge of facts indicating that such dividend, stock purchase or redemption was unlawful under this chapter, in proportion to the amounts received by such stockholders respectively.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 174(c) (src:609)
GIVEN `a claim has been successfully asserted against the director under section 174` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amount the director paid as a result of the claim` IS A NUMBER
      `the stockholder received the dividend, or assets for the sale or redemption of the stock, with knowledge of facts indicating it was unlawful under this chapter` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amount the stockholder received` IS A NUMBER
      `the total amounts received by all stockholders who received with that knowledge` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 174(c) the amount of the corporation's rights against the stockholder to which the director is subrogated` `a claim has been successfully asserted against the director under section 174` `the amount the director paid as a result of the claim` `the stockholder received the dividend, or assets for the sale or redemption of the stock, with knowledge of facts indicating it was unlawful under this chapter` `the amount the stockholder received` `the total amounts received by all stockholders who received with that knowledge` MEANS
    IF     `a claim has been successfully asserted against the director under section 174`
       AND `the stockholder received the dividend, or assets for the sale or redemption of the stock, with knowledge of facts indicating it was unlawful under this chapter`
       AND (`the total amounts received by all stockholders who received with that knowledge` GREATER THAN 0)
    THEN JUST (`the amount the director paid as a result of the claim` TIMES (`the amount the stockholder received` DIVIDED BY `the total amounts received by all stockholders who received with that knowledge`))
    ELSE NOTHING
